  "title": "Inverse Variation",
  "body": " Inverse Variation  Wrapping Paper  The marketing department for a paper company is testing wrapping paper rolls in various dimensions to see which shape consumers prefer. All the rolls contain the same amount of wrapping paper.    Width (feet)  2  2.5  3  Length (feet)  12  9.6  8  Length Feet      1(a) Point out that not every decreasing function represents inverse variation; we must test for .   Compute the product of the length and width for each roll of wrapping paper. What is the constant of inverse proportionality?  Express the length, of the paper as a function of the width, of the roll.  Sketch a graph of the function. Which basic graph does your answer resemble?  grid [0,8]x[0,20]     Ocean Temperature  The thermocline is a layer of ocean water where the temperature changes rapidly. The table shows the temperature of the water as a function of depth in the thermocline. What is the ocean temperature at a depth of 500 meters?    Depth (m)  200  400  1000  Temperature ( C)  20  10  4    How do you know from the table that this is an inverse variation?  Find a formula for , temperature, in terms of , depth.  What is the ocean temperature at a depth of 500 meters?    Sunshine  The intensity, , of radiation from the Sun is inversely proportional to the square of the distance, , from the Sun. Mercury is about 36 million miles from the Sun and receives radiation intensity of approximately 9000 watts per square meter.   Write a formula for as a function of .  The distance from the Sun to Earth is about three times the distance from the Sun to Mercury. What level of radiation intensity does Earth receive?  What happens to the radiation intensity if the distance from the Sun is quadrupled?    Checkpoint   How can you recognize inverse variation from a graph?  What should you compute to see if varies inversely with ?  Is every decreasing function an inverse variation? Explain.  In Activity 2, what happens to when you double ?   "
